The primary and sources JARs contain Code Integrity Guard classes, source, and project resources; they do not embed third-party Maven dependency classes. Dependencies listed in the POMs are separate components distributed by their respective publishers and remain subject to their own licenses and notices.

The Javadoc JAR is generated by the JDK standard doclet and includes the jQuery and jQuery UI assets supplied by the selected JDK. Their upstream license notices, including versions and copyright information, are copied unmodified from that same JDK into `legal/jquery.md` and `legal/jqueryUI.md`; the jQuery UI notice also describes CC0-licensed demo code. The build copies the exact JDK `java.base` LICENSE, ADDITIONAL_LICENSE_INFO, and ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION texts into the Javadoc `legal/` directory, alongside the notices from that JDK installation. The JDK source files are not edited. These JDK notices accompany the generated doclet materials; their presence is not a legal determination about project licensing.
